nce products; and funding agreements and pension risk transfer (PRT) solutions. Further, it engages in the real estate brokerage business. Fidelity National Financial, Inc. was incorporated in 2005 and is headquartered in Jacksonville, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Joseph Nolan | Chief Executive Officer | Age 65 | Compensation: $5.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 24K people. Revenue per employee of $589K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Fidelity National Financial, In is a large-cap financial services business with a $11.8B market cap on $14.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 8% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 5.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented ind